# OpenShift-compatible rebuild of the upstream Claude Code sandbox image.
#
# OpenShell 0.1.2's Kubernetes driver runs the workspace-init step (which
# seeds a sandbox's persistent /sandbox volume from the image) as a
# namespace-derived, non-predictable UID *and* GID on OpenShift — e.g.
# 1000910000:1000910000, read from the openshift.io/sa.scc.uid-range
# annotation (confirmed in NVIDIA's own docs, both /latest/ and the
# version-pinned /v0.1.2/ copy of kubernetes/openshift.md). The upstream
# image's /sandbox is 0770, owned 1001:0 (the standard OpenShift "arbitrary
# UID, group 0" convention) — readable by UID 1001 or group 0, neither of
# which matches the random identity OpenShell assigns, so seeding fails
# with "Permission denied (os error 13)" and the sandbox never starts.
#
# Since neither the UID nor the GID is predictable at build time, group
# tricks don't help here — the fix is to make the seeded content world-
# readable instead. Confirmed live against a real 0.1.2 gateway on
# OpenShift: this one-line fix reaches Ready and `claude --version` runs
# successfully. See docs/openshell-0.1.2-upgrade.md for the full
# root-cause writeup.
#
# Build and push:
#   podman build -t quay.io/atarazana/claude-sandbox:0.4.0 \
#     -t quay.io/atarazana/claude-sandbox:latest \
#     -f demos/keycloak-oidc/images/claude-sandbox/Containerfile \
#     demos/keycloak-oidc/images/claude-sandbox/
#   podman push quay.io/atarazana/claude-sandbox:0.4.0
#   podman push quay.io/atarazana/claude-sandbox:latest
#
# Bump the FROM tag here when a newer upstream claude-sandbox release
# ships, and re-run the build/push above.
FROM quay.io/aipcc/agentic-ci/claude-sandbox:0.4.0

USER root
RUN chmod -R a+rX /sandbox
USER sandbox
